# chained cross-lib — the MIDDLE library
library "Sib".

// "Sib Chained" is a boolean composition with its OWN cross-lib operand (`"Third"."Third Flag"`). Sib's OWN emit
// proves it total (Sib's family arm resolves Third via the index), so Sib emits "Sib Chained" as a bare total
// boolean. But the pre-emit index projects "Sib Chained" NON-total (it runs the uniform resolver, under which
// Third's operand is inert) — the Option-(a) conservative projection.

concept "Sib Cond":
- type is Condition.
- shape is RecordSet.
- coded from "Sib VS".

concept "Sib Local":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as exists ( "Sib Cond" ).

concept "Sib Chained":
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( "Third"."Third Flag" and "Sib Local" ).

terminology "Sib VS":
- valueset is `urn:sib-vs`.

activity "Sib Refer":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

decision "Sib Triage":
- when "Sib Chained" then recommend activity "Sib Refer".
